+# Carry-Forward Inventory
+
+## Core idea
+
+An empty travel case becomes a four-part inventory board. Each category adds a
+distinct asset to the case until the closing view proves that a career change is
+not a return to zero, but a move made with useful weight already packed.
+
+## Visual story
+
+1. Open on one direct question and an outlined carry case.
+2. Define the inventory as a practical, structured tool.
+3. Contrast what stays behind with the larger set of portable assets.
+4. Build four color-coded inventory compartments in sequence.
+5. Revisit all four as a completed checklist.
+6. Close by replacing a large zero with the full carry-forward case.
+
+The composition uses flat editorial illustration, crisp typography, generous
+negative space, and a restrained navy, blue, gold, and paper palette. Motion is
+purposeful: items slide into the case, dividers draw on, and checkmarks confirm
+progress. Nothing loops indefinitely.
+
