+# Design: Building Your Carry-Forward Inventory
+
+## Frame system
+
+- 1920 × 1080 canvas with a 120px content inset and a quiet 120px footer.
+- Deep navy background; paper cards and pale blue compartments supply contrast.
+- Gold signals selection and completion. Blue marks structure and connection.
+- Proxima Nova with system sans-serif fallback; no body copy below 40px.
+- A small program label and progress rail remain fixed as visual furniture.
+
+## Illustration language
+
+The central object is an editorial, geometric carry case. Its handle, shell,
+dividers, tags, and asset symbols are drawn with CSS and simple inline SVG.
+Each category owns one symbol: tool spark, compass heart, linked people, and an
+eye with a pattern ray. The symbols are descriptive rather than decorative.
+
+## Motion
+
+- Entrances settle within 1.2 seconds using short fades, rises, and scale draws.
+- Category dividers draw from left to right; assets arrive one at a time.
+- Transitions move the current card out before the next card enters.
+- The final zero recedes while the packed case advances, then holds.
+- Motion is driven by one paused, seekable timeline and has no infinite loops.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+All meaningful text is high contrast, large, and supported by shape rather than
+color alone. The narration remains verbatim in timed clips and visual density is
+kept low enough for each idea to read at a glance.
+
